# CSS Conventions

## Token sources (priority)

1. Semantic CSS variables from `src/framework/design-system/theme/tokens.css` — `--app-canvas-bg`, `--app-input-border`, `--app-text-primary`, etc.
2. Ink / brand tokens — `--ink-*`, `--primary-action`, `--system-red`, `--system-green`.
3. Never introduce a new hardcoded hex when an existing token fits.

## Global vs component styles

| Location | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `theme/tokens.css` | `:root` and `html[data-theme='dark']` variables, base `html`/`body` |
| `src/app/globals.css` | App-wide imports / resets that belong at the Next root |
| `{Component}.module.css` | Component-scoped styles only |

Import tokens once from the app layout / globals — components consume `var(--...)`.

## CSS modules

```css
.button {
  background: var(--primary-action);
  color: var(--ink-white);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
}
```

- camelCase class exports consumed as `styles.primaryAction`.
- Prefer composing classes in TS (`[styles.a, condition && styles.b].filter(Boolean).join(' ')`).
- Nesting: keep shallow (≤ 3 levels).

## Rem sizing

`html { font-size: 62.5%; }` so `1rem ≈ 10px`. Use rem for spacing, type, and control heights to match Angular Unity UI.

## Dark mode

Theme toggles `html[data-theme='dark']`. Component CSS should use semantic tokens that already change under that selector — avoid `html[data-theme='dark']` forks inside every module unless a one-off exception is required.

## What not to do

- Do not add Bootstrap component CSS; layout spacing is custom / flex / CSS modules.
- Do not style raw `<button>` / `<input>` in features when `@design-system` already provides the control.
